// current code, Kafka Streams 4.3.2
StreamsBuilder builder = new StreamsBuilder();
builder.stream("subscriptions", Consumed.with(Serdes.String(), subscriptionSerde))
       .groupBy((subscriptionId, sub) -> sub == null ? null : sub.plan(), Grouped.with(Serdes.String(), subscriptionSerde))
       .count(Materialized.as("plan-counts-store"))
       .toStream()
       .to("plan-counts", Produced.with(Serdes.String(), Serdes.Long()));

subscriptions: compacted, 12 partitions, key = subscription id, value = Subscription{customerId, plan, startedAt} from CDC;
a plan change is a new record for the same key, a cancellation is a tombstone (null value).
